    </node>
    <node id="&quot;{1,3,4}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An invalid permutation due to missing integers and inclusion of values outside the 1~n range, illustrating a violation of the permutation completeness constraint."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-522813e50d2e43c2f3a90462ea89a27d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAD: ENUMERATION_AND_SORTING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The low score indicates the student likely failed to correctly implement sorting logic or element position tracking after sorting, suggesting misunderstanding in enumeration or sorting mechanics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student enumerates over matrix indices but misapplies the logic for counting valid conditions, suggesting confusion in systematic enumeration and conditional accumulation across dimensions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student sorts intervals by (l, r) but does not sort by r as the primary key, which can lead to incorrect assignments; a correct greedy solution requires sorting by r (or r then l) to ensure optimal assignment — indicating a flawed understanding of sorting order in greedy interval problems."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student sorts the array and enumerates pairs via nested loops, but the logic only checks divisors of a[i] and XORs them with a[i], ignoring the requirement that i &lt; j and pairs must be distinct elements from the array — this leads to incorrect counting of unordered pairs and misses valid pairs where a_j &lt; a_i."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c0621f867e87fb25088a534465259d65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0d1d95f57ac4a2069ff146ad2eb612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2fe3a0bbcef55cf31ca985ee9806595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21983701d088d29b7d160b499bd3124a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAD: GREEDY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The student's greedy implementation fails to guarantee a valid permutation when multiple intervals could accept the same value; it does not check if l exceeds r for any interval, and does not backtrack or use a priority queue for available values — showing incomplete grasp of greedy constraints in permutation construction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b0d1d95f57ac4a2069ff146ad2eb612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1~N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1~n 表示排列中允许使用的整数范围，是构造排列的全局数值空间，可视为逻辑上的‘数字地理区域’。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e64500d38508ef201c017c6abd4e1b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;排列构造&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"排列构造是本题要求完成的核心任务，即在给定区间约束下，将 1~n 的整数各用一次排列成合法数组。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e64500d38508ef201c017c6abd4e1b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;贪心算法&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"学生程序使用贪心策略：按左端点排序后，依次为每个位置分配当前最小可用整数，是解决此问题的典型方法。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e64500d38508ef201c017c6abd4e1b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;排序&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"学生程序对区间按左端点 l 进行排序，是贪心策略的前提步骤，确保处理顺序的合理性。"&lt;SEP&gt;"排序是学生程序中采用的预处理步骤，将数组元素按升序排列，以便系统性地枚举可能的区间乘2方案。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5d38e5622408383b4738c3d567bf0a9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e64500d38508ef201c017c6abd4e1b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;错误答案&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"错误答案指学生程序在某些输入下输出 -1 或错误排列，表明其贪心逻辑存在缺陷，未能覆盖所有合法解情况。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e64500d38508ef201c017c6abd4e1b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1 ~ N&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1 ~ n 表示排列中允许使用的整数范围，作为数值空间的地理边界，限定排列元素的合法取值区间。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-57aa2fab03045a4f1a94b22bda9b2d8c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTROL_STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">The CONTROL_STRUCTURE is a sophisticated programming framework designed to manage decision-making and iterative control flow within a matrix-based algorithm that tracks the movement and evaluation of '1's in a grid. It incorporates a rich array of fundamental and advanced programming constructs, including nested for-loops, if-statements, while-loops (notably a while(T--) loop for handling multiple test cases), boolean flags (f, flag), and algorithmic patterns resembling BFS-style traversal to evaluate adjacent zero cells. The structure employs complex conditional logic—such as i == j (diagonal checks), i + j - 1 == 3 (anti-diagonal checks), n ≤ m, n − m &gt; 26, m == 1, and if(l ≥ l_i &amp;&amp; l ≤ r_i)—to encode rules governing grid traversal and state transitions, demonstrating a clear architectural intent and advanced understanding of control flow design.

However, despite its technically ambitious and structurally diverse implementation, the CONTROL_STRUCTURE contains critical logical and operational flaws that severely compromise its correctness, reliability, and alignment with the problem specification. Key implementation errors include: (1) improper synchronization between inner while-loops and coordinate increment variables (cnti, cntj), leading to infinite loops, skipped positions, or premature termination; (2) inconsistent resetting of loop counters and state variables, resulting in unpredictable state transitions; (3) misuse of variables such as mid[1] and mid[2] as indices without bounds or type validation, revealing a partial but erroneous grasp of control-data interactions; and (4) in the BFS component, adjacent zero checks (a[vx][vy] == 0) are performed without prior out-of-bounds validation, risking undefined behavior or incorrect counting.

Furthermore, the CONTROL_STRUCTURE includes logically unjustified and spec-incompatible conditions that reflect fundamental misunderstandings of the problem requirements. Notably, it unconditionally terminates the program with exit(1) when m == 1—an arbitrary decision unsupported by the problem specification, which instead demands a logical output (e.g., 'NO') to preserve program integrity. The condition n − m &gt; 26 is applied without algorithmic justification, suggesting an ad hoc constraint misaligned with the problem’s intended scope. Additional erroneous logic includes the use of min(0ll, 2*m - n) and n &lt;= m checks that incorrectly classify valid matrix configurations as invalid, leading to wrong outputs. Critically, the initialization m = n conflates distinct input and operational variables</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64a0b2fc78e14ac24b3790b183153e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-894984c1101b01ce3f960a1ef34f426a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa0781f7cefac10e68ae2462b8b87c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb8ee034f3f855cc75e56f09fb5d38e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db56fdcd4cd90d637f9116210b9583eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58405284c20a01544e57eb86dc25e81f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a05ba9bc76ab3827c29ee7fb9d92b0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f44ccaba75ddd991df3ba87881e905b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-465db4ec94fa4f2a3c4c7e2cee8d5ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c87648c8f1869fb042a3290df6eeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb1e0de0dc9a052c0705514de52b278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24e64575422fca0e0f51cc22d5cd223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e14c1d7f404ce9578e01e19f11a846b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2c13e4dc0c5ffdeff6ad422bae25f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c9ab832b90cad70f560049e7a740427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede3f2ca6120cc400df50c87dd9d424e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2fe3a0bbcef55cf31ca985ee9806595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3873516dc37339412e6d863d6c0b47f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e6c43b922d66931de72f56a647cc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5667e6d6ac2a6898d54282e5227a0e3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cf7f0bfd527dd66d9327c11fa6b3ebc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab516531ae70002b07e7282cf9f96ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81b34a546caa05527bcea45d142d3a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea00e0f2c81dc0fc8cf34f9d8c29edd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2ab00662c0bb8d2a07a4e1590d70a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13d0c437f60ca3acd04da12cb2b56d6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c1010a5001bece4042095877f6a8d42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f665337d67097145c49cecab1e3e3e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-886d290d1e72e5c4612a7a2f92b3deda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c9e21c9bd682aec8ed5433b29254d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57aa2fab03045a4f1a94b22bda9b2d8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6025949968addfd629ffba156975574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c900fee450edfcc61df8a5dc49da1d44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa247fbd5005d5da8b7a8cde9c6045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ba71498d3f8470570296343c8c189b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c8d7110bbe4727ef096bd8998e9b640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc7bcf65aa4562f02e59c3d8969ea961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a57838963dbbc9472322e841bbb48518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6287ae975db0cf87e45226a926715f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d16d0dd871aa1289650bde0921622&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bfa74d3cde642ef5d69d9445bbe6168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb26b30f621e23f24679fbe24e9ff02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-751de14de4f6fd0795902684f69fa4d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f50176f8b78d245242c999fcfe00f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9993599a98c4a13ce90be07d75f3c76e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-822eea5aa72002e3d106bf0be08669dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eead988a81ce4ca9e3ae8f503d1cfe1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf87c7e9ad9d433d6f2ea0161bd510c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34990b1b85de7de8bbd3a8165873d9e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-972c1235e56631f6877f43a073c916ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c7dfd3259ceb2fa5de7585826b8c564</data>
