    <node id="&quot;A_I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a_i denotes the i-th element in the array, acting as a discrete point in a numerical space; collectively, all a_i form the geometric domain from which pairs are selected for the xor-gcd condition."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i denotes the i-th element in the integer array, representing a point in a numerical space used for pairwise XOR and GCD computations."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i represents the i-th element in the sequence, a random variable uniformly distributed over [l_i, r_i], central to the computation of the sequence's value and its expectation."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i represents the i-th element of the sequence, randomly generated within interval [l_i, r_i]; it is a key variable in the definition of val(a), and its stochastic nature is central to the problem’s probability framework."&lt;SEP&gt;"a_i represents the i-th element of the sequence, a random integer variable constrained within the interval [l_i, r_i], forming the core data structure of the problem."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20a84c0c02b3b7d3ef7caf0684c1b178&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b596842b3f70ab70e198d8ac72878311&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7b2af6a814bb455302a627bfc1141e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0912d8b8a7e5a597e50db3ea5336268a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-292b69dd280ff7c3c431c909f2fa1f47</data>
    </node>
