    <node id="&quot;CNT[A[I]]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"cnt[a[i]] is a frequency counter mapping each unique value to its occurrence count, enabling efficient pair counting over the numerical domain without reprocessing duplicates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-292b69dd280ff7c3c431c909f2fa1f47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;M&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-2643532bc65acd10b75f38bdb35830ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab3ebf5f1287dbbf9a2ec35fad95eea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2076568b2623a983fd25582f3fa50c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4117c59b410de1711656865bd10cb59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb0afca86b9a6d34b643302669895ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113dd897ceb7d892e27e4255ac1852cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3873516dc37339412e6d863d6c0b47f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94a277024978e1e9676408dfab4dc3fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3220ac1e2b38ea3962a2cf303acd6f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb9086dce37a69e62b6fe93d738da78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2d96c31e95bd2cc22d83070842cc3b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c278038d1b5c766243692d5b0c40bf8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-292b69dd280ff7c3c431c909f2fa1f47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c8d7110bbe4727ef096bd8998e9b640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc7bcf65aa4562f02e59c3d8969ea961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fcdbc4a46340504623e14c8b57c676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411bbe91994001030c7a545311f4d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89dd6bd1e7fef4152822627f117d0a69</data>
      <data key="d1">"m代表查询次数，是问题中另一个关键的数值参数，表示需要独立处理的区间排序查询数量。"&lt;SEP&gt;The entity "m" is a context-dependent parameter that serves distinct functional roles across different algorithmic domains, and must not be conflated with the unrelated uppercase entity "M," which denotes the maximum possible value range for array elements in memory-constrained contexts. In string processing problems involving the evaluation of "可爱度" (cuteness/loveliness), "m" represents the exact target numerical value that a substring or subsequence must achieve; it acts as a constraint for determining whether a string meets a specified aesthetic or numerical criterion, functioning as the goal state in a search or matching algorithm. In grid-based or matrix-based problems—particularly those modeling a “battlefield” for the ability “Dragon’s Breath”—"m" denotes the number of columns in a 2D grid, working in tandem with "n" (the number of rows) to define the spatial dimensions of the problem space; in this context, "m" governs loop bounds, boundary conditions, and the horizontal extent of traversal or diagonal coverage algorithms, and misalignment with "n" can cause logical or runtime errors. Separately, in arithmetic transformation problems involving a student program referred to as “小L” (small L), "m" is the target numerical value that small L aims to reach by applying a sequence of operations to an initial value "n"; here, "m" serves as the desired final state against which intermediate results are compared to determine success. These three interpretations—target cuteness value, grid column count, and target arithmetic state—are mutually exclusive and domain-specific, with no inherent contradiction when properly contextualized. Thus, "m" is not a universal constant but a versatile parameter whose meaning is entirely determined by the problem domain in which it is used.</data>
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;双生数组&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">“双生数组”是一个特定的数组状态或数学构造，其定义要求数组的长度（或大小）为偶数，且恰好包含两种不同的元素，每种元素的出现次数相等。这一状态被多个描述一致地认定为问题或题目中要求达成的目标状态，常作为算法或数学问题的核心目标。尽管部分描述使用“数学/算法事件概念”“数学构造事件”或“特定的数组状态事件”等略有差异的术语，但其核心条件——偶数长度、两种不同元素、各出现次数相等——在所有描述中完全一致，无实质矛盾。因此，“双生数组”可被综合定义为：一种满足长度为偶数、仅含两种不同元素且每种元素出现频次相同的数组结构，是相关问题中旨在通过变换或操作所实现的最优或目标状态。</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20ddc86ac0009d54376fa7021861c400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24e64575422fca0e0f51cc22d5cd223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9224b862712b828a49a7af0256744a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f665337d67097145c49cecab1e3e3e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce2daaa3fa89648dcc0d0bc91f132ea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba89973533fbfc1f9082a792c162c21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a065cc265cc5e7c843684d7a8f2e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52330c48254eb28040891fc6658900e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c70453a05eddbb7fbeb8e33aece214f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9df1d2463f063a1f6d5c14e8234cc8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13ec9ea4c664af3656c0682232565f07</data>
    </node>
