    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"No entities of type organization, person, geo, or event are present in the input text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No geographic location is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No geographic location is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No organization is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No person is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No specific event is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No organization is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No person is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No specific event is mentioned; the text refers to a general evaluation process for student programs and error descriptions."&lt;SEP&gt;"No event is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No geographic location is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No organization is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No person is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No geographic location is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No organization is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No specific person is mentioned in the text; references are generic (e.g., 'the student')."&lt;SEP&gt;"No geographic location is mentioned or implied in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No organization is mentioned or implied in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No specific person is mentioned or implied in the text; references are generic (e.g., 'the student')."&lt;SEP&gt;"No event mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No geographic location mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No person mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No geographic location is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No organization is mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"No person is mentioned in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e63727f4e6de917ca04b71090f90f193&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ddefa42729e616016f9b54b2d45d2ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e07c5bb813fafb6e0bf55ab6101dafc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c99dbe41c2510b20494b2f7fd5ba7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d72522a7ee87f95568a6de0f128289af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3ecf33dc047b7d1aeaea74b69b6556a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a5929a39794dd8b9be93c2d9f459360&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7672123571a311714af632b0f50d801e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVALUATION PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The evaluation process is an independent assessment of a student's program and associated error description, conducted to determine correctness, logic, or performance without external bias."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of independently assessing student programs and their associated error descriptions, likely within an educational or grading context."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11fe621a78672955859dc64967ef6101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a5929a39794dd8b9be93c2d9f459360</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;双生双宿之错&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'双生双宿之错'是该算法题目的标题，象征着将数组转化为双生数组过程中存在的对称性与平衡性挑战，是问题的命名事件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"'双生双宿之错'是该问题的标题，象征将数组转换为双生数组的过程中的挑战与错误，代表问题的核心目标与抽象主题。"&lt;SEP&gt;"'双生双宿之错'是该问题的标题，象征将数组转换为双生数组过程中可能发生的错误或挑战，代表问题的叙事背景。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce2daaa3fa89648dcc0d0bc91f132ea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ddc86ac0009d54376fa7021861c400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9224b862712b828a49a7af0256744a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"mid是学生程序中用于表示数组中位数或候选值的变量名，代表学生在算法设计中试图确定目标值的核心变量，但其使用方式存在逻辑混乱。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce2daaa3fa89648dcc0d0bc91f132ea2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MID2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"mid2是学生程序中用于存储最终选定目标值的变量，其赋值逻辑依赖于多个候选mid值的比较，但未正确处理双生数组的约束条件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce2daaa3fa89648dcc0d0bc91f132ea2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A[I]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"a[i]是学生程序中表示数组元素的变量，代表输入数据的每一个数值，是学生进行绝对差值计算和目标值匹配的基本操作对象。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce2daaa3fa89648dcc0d0bc91f132ea2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PI SUM[5]&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PI sum[5]是学生程序中用于存储不同候选目标值对应操作次数和索引的结构数组，代表学生尝试多候选策略的算法设计，但实现存在越界和逻辑错误。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ce2daaa3fa89648dcc0d0bc91f132ea2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORIGINAL ENTITY EXTRACTION PROMPT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The original entity extraction prompt is a reference to a task or instruction used for extracting entities from text, which is being discussed in the context of evaluation or comparison of submissions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-676b80a33efec9486dac2ad40fd0dadb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record ID is an internal identifier system used to track submissions or records, likely part of an institutional or administrative framework for managing evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Record ID is an organizational system identifier used to uniquely track and reference individual knowledge extraction entries within a larger data management framework."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-676b80a33efec9486dac2ad40fd0dadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0fe469f0b31315b1804ec571d8c427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIMESTAMP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Timestamp is an organizational metadata standard used to log the exact date and time of record creation, ensuring chronological tracking and auditability of evaluations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Timestamp refers to the specific date and time (2025-01-21 16:28:21) when the record was logged, marking the occurrence of a submission or system event in the evaluation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-676b80a33efec9486dac2ad40fd0dadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0fe469f0b31315b1804ec571d8c427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STUDENT'S PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An informal organizational entity representing the student's computational or academic project environment, associated with an error incident."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student's program is the software or algorithm developed by a student to perform entity extraction, which is being evaluated against the original prompt for accuracy and effectiveness."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-676b80a33efec9486dac2ad40fd0dadb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a59784eb0e438c2be374884ef3182f5c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIFFERENT SUBMISSIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-676b80a33efec9486dac2ad40fd0dadb</data>
      <data key="d1">"The original entity extraction prompt is the basis for evaluating different submissions of the same problem, indicating its central role in the assessment process."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 39-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record ID: 39-2 is an event identifier associated with a timestamped record of an evaluation process regarding a student's program and error description on January 21, 2025."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11fe621a78672955859dc64967ef6101</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;哈希&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"哈希用于统计数组中各元素的出现次数，学生使用unordered_map实现频次计数，正确应用了该数据结构。"&lt;SEP&gt;"哈希被用于实现访问状态的O(1)查找，通过unordered_set避免重复状态，是优化搜索效率的关键技术应用。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8777998ec25d22d1bd1539ed5e957781&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52330c48254eb28040891fc6658900e2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;贪心&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"KNOWLEDGE_POINT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"学生程序试图通过选取使绝对差之和最小的中位数作为目标值，属于贪心策略，但未正确处理双生数组的约束（仅允许两种元素），导致逻辑错误。"&lt;SEP&gt;"贪心策略用于选择频次最高的两种元素作为目标值，学生试图保留最大频次的两个值并最小化修改次数，但逻辑错误导致贪心应用不当。"&lt;SEP&gt;"学生程序采用贪心策略：优先填充'a'，仅在必要时切换字符，试图最小化字符多样性以满足可爱度约束，但该贪心策略未正确建模问题本质，导致错误。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93f661a79bff9e316801a96e64c29dc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52330c48254eb28040891fc6658900e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ddc86ac0009d54376fa7021861c400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 41-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record ID: 41-1 refers to a specific student submission recorded on 2025-01-21 at 16:41:21, representing an instance of performance evaluation on a problem submission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f40243f32ee564d32d9c3cdd1ac7b983</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM SUBMISSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An instance of a student submitting a solution to a specific problem, evaluated independently for performance, code quality, and error analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f40243f32ee564d32d9c3cdd1ac7b983</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVALUATION SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An implied system or institution responsible for assessing student submissions based on program output and error descriptions, likely part of an educational platform."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f40243f32ee564d32d9c3cdd1ac7b983</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;中位数&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"中位数是学生程序中用于计算最小操作次数的核心数学概念，程序试图通过选取数组中位数或其邻近值作为目标值来最小化绝对差之和，但存在逻辑错误。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20ddc86ac0009d54376fa7021861c400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;绝对差之和&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"绝对差之和是衡量将数组元素调整为目标值所需操作次数的数学指标，学生程序中多次使用std::abs(a[i] - mid)计算该值，是贪心策略的基础。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20ddc86ac0009d54376fa7021861c400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;数组分割&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"学生程序将数组分为前半部分和后半部分（i &lt;= n/2 和 i &gt; n/2），并分别统计与目标值的匹配情况，意图实现双生数组的两组均衡分配，但逻辑存在缺陷。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20ddc86ac0009d54376fa7021861c400</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;41-2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"41-2 appears to be a record identifier, possibly representing a system, lab, or institutional unit involved in evaluating student programs and errors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-470b1b64a1d950c7b3b6c987e4a737e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-21 16:41:21&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The timestamp 2025-01-21 16:41:21 marks a specific instance when a student's program and error description were evaluated, indicating a discrete evaluation event."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-470b1b64a1d950c7b3b6c987e4a737e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVALUATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Evaluation is the act of analyzing a student's submission and error description to determine their grasp of relevant concepts, logged at the timestamp 2025-01-24 16:44:17."&lt;SEP&gt;"The evaluation is the process of independently assessing a student's program and error description to determine correctness, learning outcomes, or areas for improvement, without bias or external influence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-470b1b64a1d950c7b3b6c987e4a737e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0fe469f0b31315b1804ec571d8c427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N 行 N 列矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"‘n 行 n 列矩阵’是问题中操作的对象，其结构由偶数行和列组成，并被划分为四个相等区域，用于判断是否为‘好矩阵’。"&lt;SEP&gt;"‘n 行 n 列矩阵’是问题中操作的对象，其结构被严格定义为仅由‘0’和‘1’构成，且需满足特定分区条件，是解题的核心数据结构。"&lt;SEP&gt;"‘n 行 n 列矩阵’是问题中的核心数据结构，具有偶数行和列，需被划分为四个相等区域，其中仅左上角为全‘1’，其余为全‘0’，是操作的目标形态。"&lt;SEP&gt;“N 行 N 列矩阵”是问题中的核心数据结构，指代一个大小为偶数阶（即行数和列数均为偶数）的正方形网格，由字符 ‘0’ 和 ‘1’ 构成。该矩阵被严格划分为四个相等的区域，其中左上角区域为全 ‘1’，其余三个区域为全 ‘0’，这一特定分区规则是定义“好矩阵”的必要条件。作为问题操作的目标对象，其合法形态完全由这一结构约束所决定，且其转换与操作是解决问题的关键。该矩阵不仅是一个抽象的数学结构，也是问题中二维字符阵列的正式表述，其属性和行为由“好矩阵”的定义严格规范，且其性质由“小红”所定义。所有描述一致确认：该矩阵必须满足偶数阶、四等分区域、左上全1、其余全0的条件，才能被视为“好矩阵”，并成为问题求解的核心焦点。&lt;SEP&gt;"该矩阵是问题的核心数据结构，由 n 行 n 列的字符 '0' 和 '1' 构成，需满足特定分区规则才能称为'好矩阵'，其性质由小红定义。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3b731333a385835804dfd4d80ce0f116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2ab00662c0bb8d2a07a4e1590d70a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44413f301feabb11269b4dc39c5222e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf97b3ffe5b076b009e7bd3766ab5ff8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-751de14de4f6fd0795902684f69fa4d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6025949968addfd629ffba156975574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f50176f8b78d245242c999fcfe00f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ae00dd7b87111567e7a60bf8a5b446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-149cbf20a38db662126124752f186e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6498d4b9b73c6042d086d98534de214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b114d72fb1df4b15a6815afb987ada0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38a167365a5d0276ffb59f1c81ca944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;好矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"好矩阵是一个数学构造事件，指满足特定条件的n×n01矩阵：行数和列数为偶数，且仅左上四分之一区域全为'1'，其余区域全为'0'。"&lt;SEP&gt;“好矩阵”是由小红定义的一种特定的 n×n 01 矩阵目标状态，其核心特征为：矩阵的行数和列数必须均为偶数，且整个矩阵被精确划分为四个大小相等的 (n/2)×(n/2) 子区域；其中，仅左上角子区域全部填充为 ‘1’，而右上、左下和右下三个子区域则全部填充为 ‘0’。这一结构具有唯一确定的二元分区模式，确保了定义的精确性与无歧义性。作为数学构造对象，“好矩阵”不仅体现了偶数维度约束与四象限分布的严格对称性，更在算法与编程问题中被明确设定为最终目标状态或终止条件。在相关问题求解过程中，学生程序需通过行交换或列交换操作，将任意给定的初始 01 矩阵转化为这一理想配置，从而判定算法是否成功。因此，“好矩阵”的本质在于其结构的唯一性与可操作性，用作规范解空间、评估算法正确性的明确标准。所有描述一致确认其定义要点，无实质矛盾，共同强化了其作为标准目标状态的权威性与清晰性。&lt;SEP&gt;"好矩阵是指满足行数和列数为偶数，且左上四分之一区域全为'1'、其余区域全为'0'的特定01矩阵构造结果，是问题要求达成的目标状态。"&lt;SEP&gt;"好矩阵是一个特定构造的n×n 01矩阵事件，要求行数和列数为偶数，且仅左上四分之一区域为'1'，其余区域全为'0'，是本题要达成的目标状态。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db8545487dac8cc471629adfdae25139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e4ddc2f7b93043f925591323e0cf949&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa0781f7cefac10e68ae2462b8b87c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb8ee034f3f855cc75e56f09fb5d38e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44413f301feabb11269b4dc39c5222e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ae00dd7b87111567e7a60bf8a5b446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb266f676f817ae1da7faf5ef3318979&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f4fbb8a3d02558286f8c4e5541d666a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38a167365a5d0276ffb59f1c81ca944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3527463f6698513f73f0ea87456339d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c87648c8f1869fb042a3290df6eeb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50782e0a3ccbda98907246d7b063785c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b731333a385835804dfd4d80ce0f116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-213863e034cdfa89c3209c59cdabf9c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ede3f2ca6120cc400df50c87dd9d424e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b114d72fb1df4b15a6815afb987ada0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-863e6c43b922d66931de72f56a647cc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99207f6dd7e45092a4cdbb095f26b994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3265a331ceecdcaa4effe7d518de46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81b34a546caa05527bcea45d142d3a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2ab00662c0bb8d2a07a4e1590d70a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6025949968addfd629ffba156975574&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c230135cc0686d17fd15b2cc48624237&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-149cbf20a38db662126124752f186e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-085095cde15602fbbadf4f1eb221b4d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8aa247fbd5005d5da8b7a8cde9c6045&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a57838963dbbc9472322e841bbb48518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bb26b30f621e23f24679fbe24e9ff02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0569105254caf9ef1ed75024750e2dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3322c36325d08c143197c29a7781bd1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf97b3ffe5b076b009e7bd3766ab5ff8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f50176f8b78d245242c999fcfe00f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7545db3cc1ccecefc971d68863f9d5d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6498d4b9b73c6042d086d98534de214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17db13cfc936b3b0723f1bccf5ab9e2b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 42-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A specific submission record identified by ID 42-1, timestamped 2025-01-21 17:27:43, containing a student's program and error description for evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e40dde04eb7b7505a46609746775a53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-21 17:27:43&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The timestamp associated with Record ID: 42-1, representing the exact moment the student's submission was recorded; serves as a temporal location in the evaluation system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e40dde04eb7b7505a46609746775a53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The program is the student's code submission, used as primary evidence to assess their technical understanding and application of concepts."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student's code or computational solution submitted as part of Record ID: 42-1, used to evaluate their technical understanding and problem-solving approach."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student's code or solution submission used to assess understanding; the primary artifact analyzed for correctness and knowledge application."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e40dde04eb7b7505a46609746775a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55785fde60a695d1127152a7469bca07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a074a38ecf5866008803eb9d3c6559bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOOD:&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A classification label used when the student's submission contains no errors or correctly addresses the problem, indicating demonstrated understanding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e40dde04eb7b7505a46609746775a53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BAD:&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A classification label used when the student's submission contains explicit errors, indicating misunderstanding or lack of understanding of the knowledge point."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0e40dde04eb7b7505a46609746775a53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KNOWLEDGE POINTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Conceptual areas of learning that may be assessed in a problem; not mentioned in the error description imply the student has mastered them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Core programming concepts or topics (e.g., loops, conditionals, data structures) that are relevant to solving the problem and must be understood by the student."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points are specific concepts, skills, or learning objectives from a curriculum or problem set that are assessed through the student's program and error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"The underlying concepts or skills being assessed in the problem; those not mentioned in the error description are inferred as mastered by the student."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to the structured concepts or skills assessed in the problem; those not mentioned in the error description are assumed to be mastered by the student."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific learning objectives or content areas in an educational context; those not mentioned in the error description are inferred as areas where the student demonstrates proficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to the specific educational concepts or skills being assessed in the student's submission; their mastery is inferred from whether errors are mentioned or not."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conceptual areas or skills assessed in the problem; those not mentioned in the error description are inferred as mastered by the student."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to the specific concepts or skills being assessed in the student's submission; those not mentioned in the error description are assumed to be well understood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points are the specific concepts or skills assessed in the problem; those not mentioned in the error description are assumed to be understood by the student."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to specific learning objectives or content areas that the student is expected to understand; their presence or absence in error descriptions determines the 'Good' or 'Bad' label."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to the specific concepts or skills being assessed in the educational problem; their presence or absence in the error description determines whether the student's understanding is marked as 'Good' or 'Bad'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge Points refer to the specific concepts or skills being assessed in an educational problem; mastery is inferred based on whether errors in the submission relate to them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge points refer to the specific concepts or skills being assessed in a problem; their presence or absence in error descriptions determines the mastery level evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15c4a600bf65356d8978132856a878e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55785fde60a695d1127152a7469bca07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0747c1df78c5777327fecd87fccd7d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1c99dbe41c2510b20494b2f7fd5ba7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7b75b911292d4622eb19f6a2ca78a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f4bd0ea17b3929365d93428c4298f84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3ecf33dc047b7d1aeaea74b69b6556a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e40dde04eb7b7505a46609746775a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37700e6b965dc09fe5f8a9761da4d8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8766ea63b59cbbc45f9300a452dd50e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38cbf6e525bbd6a2cabb176b11d77cb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad053ae13cd059fe9b4184d3384bebe2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725789acf7c08a6f0c7c8cab1e7f5ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b80c6952ceb5bde1a528cf5c85d2c25a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASTERY LEVEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An evaluative metric derived from the student's program and error description, reflecting their grasp of the specific problem and submission, used to track learning progress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastery Level is an evaluative metric derived from student performance on a specific problem, reflecting their understanding of targeted knowledge points."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastery level is an assessment of the student's proficiency on a specific problem, derived directly from the error description and aligned with the 'Good' or 'Bad' indicators."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mastery level is an evaluative metric reflecting the student's performance on this specific problem and submission, determined by analyzing their program and error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastery level is a qualitative or quantitative assessment of the student’s grasp of the concept(s) tested in the problem, derived solely from the error description and submission content."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mastery level is an evaluative metric reflecting the student’s proficiency on the specific problem and submission, derived from the application of 'Good' or 'Bad' labels and error analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastery level is an evaluative metric derived from the analysis of a student’s submission and error description, reflecting their grasp of the problem’s knowledge points on a per-submission basis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mastery level is a diagnostic classification (Good/Bad) derived from the analysis of the error description and the presence or absence of knowledge points in the submission."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0747c1df78c5777327fecd87fccd7d6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c80b6ec9209aca37eecb346184a349b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0fe469f0b31315b1804ec571d8c427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e40dde04eb7b7505a46609746775a53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37700e6b965dc09fe5f8a9761da4d8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8766ea63b59cbbc45f9300a452dd50e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725789acf7c08a6f0c7c8cab1e7f5ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b80c6952ceb5bde1a528cf5c85d2c25a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 43-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Record ID: 43-1 refers to a specific student submission recorded on 2025-01-21 17:29:29, used for evaluating understanding based on program and error description."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a074a38ecf5866008803eb9d3c6559bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-21 17:29:29&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Timestamp marking the exact time of the student submission associated with Record ID: 43-1, used to track and evaluate individual performance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a074a38ecf5866008803eb9d3c6559bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVALUATOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The evaluator is the entity (likely an instructor or automated system) responsible for analyzing the student's program and error description to determine mastery level and understanding."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a074a38ecf5866008803eb9d3c6559bb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KNOWLEDGE POINT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A knowledge point is a specific skill, fact, or concept that may be tested in a problem; its presence or absence in the error description indicates whether the student has demonstrated understanding or not."&lt;SEP&gt;"A knowledge point refers to a specific concept or skill being tested in the student's program; each is evaluated as understood ('Good') or misunderstood ('Bad') based on the error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"Knowledge Point refers to a defined concept or principle from the provided list that is evaluated for student understanding in the context of an educational assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"A knowledge point refers to a specific skill, concept, or learning objective that the student is expected to demonstrate mastery of in their submission; absence of errors implies understanding, while errors imply misunderstanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"A knowledge point refers to a specific skill, concept, or piece of information that the student is expected to demonstrate mastery of in their submission; unmentioned knowledge points are assumed to be understood."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a074a38ecf5866008803eb9d3c6559bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26b0d0ed2ff7cae6f89f08cce6fe3a3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c80b6ec9209aca37eecb346184a349b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e25d2145ec23366f1eef2a7d47f3400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd0fe469f0b31315b1804ec571d8c427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;44-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"44-1 is a record identifier for a student submission, likely used for tracking academic performance or error analysis in an educational context."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7b75b911292d4622eb19f6a2ca78a63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-21 17:30:35&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"2025-01-21 17:30:35 is a timestamp marking the exact time of submission for record ID 44-1, indicating when the student's program and error description were logged."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7b75b911292d4622eb19f6a2ca78a63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM CONTEXT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Problem context refers to the instructional or computational environment in which the student's program is evaluated, containing relevant knowledge points and expected behaviors for assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refers to the general framework or setting in which the student's programming problem is situated, potentially involving educational or institutional structures."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7b75b911292d4622eb19f6a2ca78a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad053ae13cd059fe9b4184d3384bebe2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VARIABLE NAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Specific identifiers used within the student's program to represent data values; their correct or incorrect usage reflects understanding of programming syntax and semantics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Variable names are identifiers used in the student's program to represent data or state, and their correct usage reflects understanding of programming syntax and semantics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7b75b911292d4622eb19f6a2ca78a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad053ae13cd059fe9b4184d3384bebe2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNCTION NAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Function names are user-defined or built-in routines in the student's program that encapsulate logic; their proper implementation indicates comprehension of modular programming and control flow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Named blocks of code defined by the student to perform specific tasks; their naming and structure indicate comprehension of modular programming principles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7b75b911292d4622eb19f6a2ca78a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad053ae13cd059fe9b4184d3384bebe2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPECIFIC PROBLEM ELEMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Key components of the programming problem such as input/output requirements, constraints, or algorithms that the student must correctly implement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Specific problem elements refer to unique components, constraints, or requirements explicitly stated in the problem statement that the student's solution must address to be considered correct."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7b75b911292d4622eb19f6a2ca78a63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad053ae13cd059fe9b4184d3384bebe2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RECORD ID: 45-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A unique identifier for a specific student submission record, used to track and reference individual evaluations in an educational assessment system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ad053ae13cd059fe9b4184d3384bebe2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIMESTAMP: 2025-01-21 17:38:26&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The precise date and time when the student submission was recorded, providing temporal context for evaluation and audit purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ad053ae13cd059fe9b4184d3384bebe2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N 行 N 列 01 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"该实体指代一个正方形网格结构，行数和列数均为偶数，由字符'0'和'1'构成，是问题中需要被转换的目标数据结构，其空间划分（左上、右上、左下、右下四个区域）是判断‘好矩阵’的核心依据。"&lt;SEP&gt;"该矩阵是问题的核心对象，具有 n 行 n 列的正方形结构，仅由字符 '0' 和 '1' 构成，需被转换为左上角为全 '1'、其余为全 '0' 的‘好矩阵’，其中 n 为偶数。"&lt;SEP&gt;"这是一个正方形的二进制矩阵，大小为 n×n（n 为偶数），由字符 '0' 和 '1' 构成，目标是通过相邻交换操作使其成为‘好矩阵’，其中仅左上四分之一区域为 '1'，其余为 '0'。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7545db3cc1ccecefc971d68863f9d5d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8545487dac8cc471629adfdae25139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f4fbb8a3d02558286f8c4e5541d666a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM SOLVING PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The process of transforming a given 01 matrix into a '好矩阵' through adjacent character swaps, constrained by a maximum operation limit of n³/2, requiring algorithmic reasoning and simulation techniques."&lt;SEP&gt;"The structured process of transforming a given 01 matrix into a '好矩阵' through adjacent character swaps, constrained by operation limits and requiring algorithmic reasoning to ensure correctness and efficiency."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db8545487dac8cc471629adfdae25139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f4fbb8a3d02558286f8c4e5541d666a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADJACENT CHARACTER SWAP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The allowed elementary operation in the problem, where two neighboring elements in the matrix (horizontally or vertically) are exchanged, used as the sole means to rearrange the matrix toward the target state."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f4fbb8a3d02558286f8c4e5541d666a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEFT-UPPER REGION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The top-left quadrant of the n×n matrix, defined by coordinates 1 ≤ i,j ≤ n/2, which must contain all '1's in a '好矩阵' and is the target region for all '1' elements to be moved into."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f4fbb8a3d02558286f8c4e5541d666a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTHER THREE REGIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The remaining three quadrants of the matrix (right-upper, left-lower, right-lower), each of size (n/2)×(n/2), which must contain only '0's in a '好矩阵' and serve as regions from which '1's must be removed."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f4fbb8a3d02558286f8c4e5541d666a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPERATION LIMIT: N³/2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The constraint on the maximum number of adjacent swaps allowed to transform the matrix, which defines the efficiency boundary for any valid solution and implies the need for an optimized approach."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f4fbb8a3d02558286f8c4e5541d666a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM STATEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The problem statement describes the task of transforming a given 01 matrix into a '好矩阵' by swapping adjacent characters, with constraints on maximum operations and guaranteed solvability, forming the core challenge of the competition problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"The problem statement describes the task of transforming a given 01 matrix into a ‘好矩阵’ using only adjacent character swaps, with constraints on maximum operations and guaranteed solvability, commonly found in algorithmic programming contests."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50782e0a3ccbda98907246d7b063785c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c230135cc0686d17fd15b2cc48624237</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;左上区域&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"左上区域指矩阵中第 1 行到第 n/2 行、第 1 列到第 n/2 列的子区域，是唯一允许包含‘1’字符的区域，是‘好矩阵’定义的核心空间结构。"&lt;SEP&gt;"指矩阵中行和列索引均在 [1, n/2] 范围内的子区域，是‘好矩阵’中唯一允许包含'1'的区域，是算法需要集中填充的目标地理区域。"&lt;SEP&gt;"矩阵中位于前 n/2 行和前 n/2 列的子区域，是‘好矩阵’中唯一允许包含'1'字符的区域，其余区域必须全为'0'。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2ab00662c0bb8d2a07a4e1590d70a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;右上区域&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"右上区域指矩阵中第 1 行到第 n/2 行、第 n/2+1 列到第 n 列的子区域，必须全为‘0’字符，是‘好矩阵’定义的约束区域之一。"&lt;SEP&gt;"指矩阵中行索引在 [1, n/2]、列索引在 [n/2+1, n] 的子区域，在‘好矩阵’中必须全为'0'，是算法需要清空的区域。"&lt;SEP&gt;"矩阵中位于前 n/2 行和后 n/2 列的子区域，在‘好矩阵’中必须全部由'0'字符构成。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2ab00662c0bb8d2a07a4e1590d70a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;左下区域&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"左下区域指矩阵中第 n/2+1 行到第 n 行、第 1 列到第 n/2 列的子区域，必须全为‘0’字符，是‘好矩阵’定义的约束区域之一。"&lt;SEP&gt;"指矩阵中行索引在 [n/2+1, n]、列索引在 [1, n/2] 的子区域，在‘好矩阵’中必须全为'0'，是算法需要清空的区域。"&lt;SEP&gt;"矩阵中位于后 n/2 行和前 n/2 列的子区域，在‘好矩阵’中必须全部由'0'字符构成。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2ab00662c0bb8d2a07a4e1590d70a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;右下区域&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"右下区域指矩阵中第 n/2+1 行到第 n 行、第 n/2+1 列到第 n 列的子区域，必须全为‘0’字符，是‘好矩阵’定义的约束区域之一。"&lt;SEP&gt;"指矩阵中行和列索引均在 [n/2+1, n] 范围内的子区域，在‘好矩阵’中必须全为'0'，是算法需要清空的区域。"&lt;SEP&gt;"矩阵中位于后 n/2 行和后 n/2 列的子区域，在‘好矩阵’中必须全部由'0'字符构成。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a2ab00662c0bb8d2a07a4e1590d70a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;相邻字符交换&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"一种允许操作者交换矩阵中水平或垂直相邻的两个字符位置的操作，是将初始矩阵转换为‘好矩阵’的唯一允许操作手段。"&lt;SEP&gt;"这是唯一允许的操作，指交换矩阵中上下或左右相邻的两个字符，是实现矩阵重构的唯一手段。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;操作次数限制&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"约束条件为操作总次数不得超过 n³/2，是问题求解的效率要求，确保算法在多项式时间内可行。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;01 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"由字符'0'和'1'构成的 n×n 方阵，是小红持有的初始输入数据，其结构可能不符合‘好矩阵’的定义，需通过交换操作修正。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e928027976f9566a19f73c1a7c62fce5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM_SOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Problem_Solution is the student's submission and associated error analysis, which serves as the basis for evaluating mastery of the listed knowledge points."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb9ecea8e462df8b8d62bff75dfff387</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2025-01-21 17:46:24&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The timestamp indicates the temporal and geographic context of the submission, though no specific location is provided, it anchors the record in time for evaluation purposes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd3a2cb8082fc545af89c60f79efbd13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;53-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"53-1 is a unique record identifier for a student submission, marking a specific instance of problem-solving activity for evaluation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd3a2cb8082fc545af89c60f79efbd13</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROGRAMMING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Programming is a broad field encompassing the creation and implementation of software systems, potentially relevant as a foundational context for the knowledge points listed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Programming is a broad field encompassing the creation and implementation of software systems; in this context, it serves as the foundational discipline underpinning the problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"Programming is the active process of writing, testing, and executing code to solve computational problems; in this context, it represents the applied activity the student engaged in."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2c44d59ce1bad68da6631b1fbb2adb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b61b86f3541688082eb6cab0bf35563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N 行 N 列 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The n×n matrix is a spatial structure in the problem domain, representing the two-dimensional grid where operations (swaps) occur; its geometric division into four quadrants is central to defining the target state."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-50782e0a3ccbda98907246d7b063785c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;左上、右上、左下、右下四个区域&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"这四个区域是将 n×n 矩阵等分后形成的几何分区，其中仅左上区域应全为 '1'，其余为 '0'，是判断矩阵是否为‘好矩阵’的空间依据。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-751de14de4f6fd0795902684f69fa4d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;交换相邻字符操作&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"这是小红允许的唯一操作，指在矩阵中交换两个相邻（上下或左右）位置的字符，用于逐步将矩阵转化为满足‘好矩阵’条件的状态。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-751de14de4f6fd0795902684f69fa4d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM_SOLUTION_SUBMISSION_56-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Problem_Solution_Submission_56-1 is the specific student submission recorded on 2025-01-21 17:48:48, which is being evaluated for mastery of algorithmic knowledge points based on correctness and error patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Problem_Solution_Submission_56-1 is the specific student submission recorded on 2025-01-21 17:48:48, which is being evaluated for mastery of algorithmic knowledge points."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bbb3792d7e38be88574653599b12f4fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM SOLVING CONTEXT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Problem Solving Context refers to the computational challenge of transforming a given 01 matrix into a ‘好矩阵’ using only adjacent character swaps, under constraints of efficiency and correctness, as presented in an educational or competitive programming setting."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Problem Solving Context refers to the scenario in which a student is tasked with transforming a 01 matrix into a ‘好矩阵’ using adjacent swaps, under constraints on operation count, and is evaluated based on program output and error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"The problem solving context refers to the scenario in which a student is tasked with transforming a given 01 matrix into a '好矩阵' using adjacent swaps, under constraints of operation count and correctness, as presented in an educational or competitive programming setting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7545db3cc1ccecefc971d68863f9d5d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ae00dd7b87111567e7a60bf8a5b446&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38a167365a5d0276ffb59f1c81ca944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;操作次数限制 \TFRAC{N^3}{2}&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"这是一个算法约束条件，要求变换矩阵的操作次数不得超过 n³/2，学生程序虽满足此上限，但未能正确实现目标状态转换。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;模拟算法&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"学生程序采用的是一种基于模拟的贪心策略，逐个将'1'移动到左上区域的指定位置，但因坐标更新逻辑错误导致移动路径混乱。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae919ec47abcddaf06ba6ba075881e6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROBLEM_SOLUTION_SUBMISSION_59-1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Problem_Solution_Submission_59-1 is the specific student submission on 2025-01-21 17:56:06, evaluated for understanding of listed knowledge points based on program correctness and error description."&lt;SEP&gt;"Problem_Solution_Submission_59-1 is the specific student submission on 2025-01-21 17:56:06, evaluated for understanding of listed knowledge points based on program correctness and error description; no errors were reported, implying correct application of all listed concepts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9fb69be12afd9f336760b13b49eb33f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;牛可乐&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"牛可乐是本题的提出者，定义了字符串‘可爱度’的概念，并设计了关于子串与不连续子序列匹配的算法问题。"&lt;SEP&gt;牛可乐是多个算法问题的提出者和定义者，在不同问题背景下扮演了核心出题者的角色。在砖块矩阵相关问题中，牛可乐定义了“蓝色极大连通块”的概念，并提出了一类优化问题：计算使特定蓝色连通块掉落所需敲碎的最少灰色砖块数量，从而构建了一个涉及图论与动态规划的算法题。同时，在字符串算法领域，牛可乐同样作为核心出题者，定义了“字符串可爱度”的概念，并设计了多个相关问题，包括：判定是否存在满足特定条件的字符串、判断连续子串与不连续子序列是否相等，以及探索子串与不连续子序列之间的匹配关系。尽管描述中涉及两类看似无关的问题（砖块矩阵与字符串可爱度），但所有来源一致表明牛可乐是这些独立问题的原创提出者与概念定义者，其角色为虚构的命题者，主导了这些算法题目的背景设定与核心定义。因此，牛可乐被统一视为一个在算法竞赛命题中提出多种类型问题的虚构出题者，涵盖图结构优化与字符串匹配两大方向。&lt;SEP&gt;"牛可乐是题目中定义字符串‘可爱度’概念的提出者，作为问题设定的作者角色。"&lt;SEP&gt;"牛可乐是本题的提出者，定义了字符串的‘可爱度’概念，并设计了关于子串与不连续子序列匹配的问题。"&lt;SEP&gt;"牛可乐是题目中的出题者，定义了字符串‘可爱度’的概念，并提出了关于是否存在满足特定条件字符串的问题。"&lt;SEP&gt;"牛可乐是题目中的出题者，定义了字符串的‘可爱度’概念，并提出了关于是否存在满足特定条件字符串的问题。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4bfa74d3cde642ef5d69d9445bbe6168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab516531ae70002b07e7282cf9f96ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93f661a79bff9e316801a96e64c29dc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc7bcf65aa4562f02e59c3d8969ea961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113dd897ceb7d892e27e4255ac1852cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c900fee450edfcc61df8a5dc49da1d44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c9ab832b90cad70f560049e7a740427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ba71498d3f8470570296343c8c189b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2076568b2623a983fd25582f3fa50c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c8d7110bbe4727ef096bd8998e9b640&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4154b1e05dbece67a8efa0eab39a9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf87c7e9ad9d433d6f2ea0161bd510c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6287ae975db0cf87e45226a926715f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad26e515beb14545a407a310ae7ac139</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;蓝色极大连通块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"蓝色极大连通块是指在矩阵中由四连通的蓝色砖块构成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是问题的核心计算目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指在砖块矩阵中，由四连通的蓝色砖块构成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指由四连通的蓝色砖块组成的最大连通区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是题目中核心的计算目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色极大连通块是指在砖块矩阵中，通过四连通（上下左右）连接的最大化蓝色砖块区域，不包含灰色砖块，其是否掉落取决于是否与灰色砖块共边，是问题的核心计算目标。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4154b1e05dbece67a8efa0eab39a9cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad26e515beb14545a407a310ae7ac139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;灰色砖块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"灰色砖块是矩阵中可被敲碎的砖块，用于移除以使蓝色极大连通块掉落，是问题中可操作的元素。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块是矩阵中可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或移除蓝色极大连通块，是计算最少敲碎数量的关键对象。"&lt;SEP&gt;"灰色砖块是矩阵中可被敲碎的砖块，用于隔离或使蓝色极大连通块掉落，是计算最少敲碎数量的关键对象。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad26e515beb14545a407a310ae7ac139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;蓝色砖块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"蓝色砖块是矩阵中不可敲碎的砖块，以蓝色斜线表示，构成蓝色极大连通块的基本单元，其连通性决定块的结构。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色砖块是矩阵中不可敲碎的砖块，通过四连通形成蓝色极大连通块，是分析掉落条件的基础元素。"&lt;SEP&gt;"蓝色砖块是矩阵中不可被敲碎的砖块，通过四连通形成蓝色极大连通块，是问题分析的核心对象。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad26e515beb14545a407a310ae7ac139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;(I,J)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify individual cells in the grid map, where i is the row (from top to bottom) and j is the column (from left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) 是用于表示砖块矩阵中第 i 行第 j 列砖块的坐标系统，是描述砖块位置和连通性的基础数学表示。"&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) 是表示矩阵中砖块位置的坐标系统，i 表示从上往下的行号，j 表示从左往右的列号，用于精确定位每个砖块的物理位置。"&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) 是矩阵中砖块的坐标表示法，用于唯一标识第 i 行第 j 列的砖块，是描述砖块位置和连通性的核心数学符号。"&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify individual cells in the grid map, where i is the row index (top to bottom) and j is the column index (left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify specific cells in the grid map, where i is the row index (top to bottom) and j is the column index (left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is the coordinate system used to identify each cell in the grid map, with i indicating row (top to bottom) and j indicating column (left to right)."&lt;SEP&gt;"(i,j) is a coordinate system used to identify individual cells in the grid map, where i is the row index (top to bottom) and j is the column index (left to right)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ad26e515beb14545a407a310ae7ac139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ab3ebf5f1287dbbf9a2ec35fad95eea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89dd6bd1e7fef4152822627f117d0a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fcdbc4a46340504623e14c8b57c676&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411bbe91994001030c7a545311f4d2a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cb0afca86b9a6d34b643302669895ff</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N \TIMES M 矩阵&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"n \times m 矩阵是题目中砖块的二维排列结构，由 n 行 m 列的砖块组成，是整个问题的物理和逻辑基础。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;四连通&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块之间是否属于同一个连通块，是识别蓝色极大连通块的核心规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指在二维网格中，一个砖块仅与上、下、左、右四个直接相邻的砖块相连，是定义蓝色极大连通块连通性的核心规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"四连通是指上下左右四个方向的相邻关系，用于定义蓝色砖块之间是否属于同一连通块，是识别蓝色极大连通块的算法基础。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad26e515beb14545a407a310ae7ac139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;共边&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"共边是指两个砖块在上下左右四个方向上共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块相邻，从而决定其是否可掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"共边是指两个砖块在上下左右方向上直接相邻共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块接触，从而决定其是否可掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"共边是指两个砖块在网格中共享一条边，用于判断蓝色极大连通块是否与灰色砖块接触，从而决定其是否可掉落。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad26e515beb14545a407a310ae7ac139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;边界上的蓝色极大连通块&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"边界上的蓝色极大连通块是指至少有一个蓝色砖块位于矩阵的最外层行或列，这类连通块的掉落条件特殊，无需考虑悬空问题。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;敲碎&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是实现蓝色极大连通块掉落的唯一手段，其最小数量是问题的求解目标。"&lt;SEP&gt;"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，目的是破坏蓝色极大连通块与周围环境的连接，使其能够掉落。"&lt;SEP&gt;"敲碎是指移除灰色砖块的操作，是实现蓝色极大连通块掉落的唯一手段，问题要求最小化该操作次数。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad26e515beb14545a407a310ae7ac139&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;悬空&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"悬空是指蓝色极大连通块边缘缺乏下方支撑，但在边界上的蓝色块不因悬空而要求额外敲碎，是边界情况的特殊处理规则。"&lt;SEP&gt;"悬空是指蓝色砖块下方或周围缺乏支撑而可能自然掉落的状态，但对于边界上的蓝色极大连通块，此状态被忽略，不作为掉落条件。"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e8858aadef99b81cf3431326cb24cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BFS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BFS (Breadth-First Search) is an algorithmic process used in the code to traverse a grid-based graph, counting connected components and adjacent zero cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"bfs is a recursive function implementing breadth-first search to explore connected components of land cells, counting reachable cells and adjacent water cells in a grid-based search space."&lt;SEP&gt;"bfs（广度优先搜索）是程序中用于遍历和识别蓝色极大连通块的算法，通过队列逐层探索相邻蓝色砖块。"&lt;SEP&gt;"BFS（广度优先搜索）是学生程序中用于探索所有可能操作路径的算法，用于判断n是否能转化为m。"&lt;SEP&gt;"BFS（广度优先搜索）是学生程序中用于探索所有可能操作路径的算法，通过队列结构系统性地遍历数字变换状态，是解决问题的核心方法。"&lt;SEP&gt;"bfs is a function in the student's program implementing breadth-first search to explore possible transformations of the number n to reach m, using queue-based state exploration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-779b6394c3bf1e24a845e4dbfebf7904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccb9086dce37a69e62b6fe93d738da78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc25d09f19797d7b290144c34c7eb8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0e2ac3fe25900f76cfe73eedcd9570d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8777998ec25d22d1bd1539ed5e957781&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4117c59b410de1711656865bd10cb59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRID TRAVERSAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Grid Traversal refers to the systematic exploration of a 2D grid using BFS to identify connected regions of 1s and count adjacent 0s, central to the problem's logic."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc25d09f19797d7b290144c34c7eb8b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAPH STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Graph Structure is implicitly represented by the 2D grid, where each cell is a node connected to its four directional neighbors (up, down, left, right), forming an unweighted graph."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc25d09f19797d7b290144c34c7eb8b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEARCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">SEARCH is a fundamental conceptual category in programming that refers to algorithmic techniques for locating elements, values, or specific conditions within data structures. It encompasses a range of well-established methods, including linear search, binary search, breadth-first search (BFS), and depth-first search (DFS), all of which are foundational for solving traversal, connectivity, and optimization problems. SEARCH is applied in practical scenarios such as identifying connected regions of 1s in a binary grid using BFS, where the algorithm correctly tracks connected components via state variables like ans1, or exhaustively scanning a 2D grid using nested loops to detect positions where a[i][j] == 1 and evaluate neighboring elements for invalid configurations. It is also used in more complex contexts, such as exploring all possible operation paths from n to m or evaluating winning sequences in game-theoretic problems involving double-move privilege, where complete traversal of the search space via BFS or DFS is essential.

Despite a generally solid conceptual understanding of SEARCH among practitioners and students, implementation errors are prevalent and often undermine its effectiveness. Critical flaws include incorrect state management—for instance, updating a global minimum variable (Min) even when the current component size (cnt1) is not the maximum—leading to erroneous optimization results. Other common mistakes involve flawed condition logic, such as incorrectly setting flags when searching for elements greater than 1 in rows, columns, or diagonals, or misattributing simple procedural operations (e.g., summing array elements without a conditional traversal criterion) as SEARCH operations, when no actual data structure exploration or condition-based search occurs. SEARCH is inapplicable in contexts resolved by direct mathematical reasoning without traversal.

Additionally, a frequent student error involves relying on single-directional reverse inference or failing to explore the full search space, demonstrating an insufficient grasp of the algorithmic breadth required for comprehensive search. While the intent behind many implementations is to detect patterns or violations through systematic scanning, these intentions are often compromised by logic errors, resulting in incorrect outputs. Therefore, successful application of SEARCH requires not only choosing the appropriate algorithmic technique (linear, binary, BFS, DFS) but also ensuring accurate state tracking, correct conditional evaluation, and exhaustive exploration of the relevant data structure. SEARCH is not explicitly marked as good or bad in the provided text, but its effectiveness is entirely contingent on proper implementation and conceptual understanding.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64a0b2fc78e14ac24b3790b183153e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-894984c1101b01ce3f960a1ef34f426a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db56fdcd4cd90d637f9116210b9583eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58405284c20a01544e57eb86dc25e81f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a05ba9bc76ab3827c29ee7fb9d92b0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f44ccaba75ddd991df3ba87881e905b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb1e0de0dc9a052c0705514de52b278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e14c1d7f404ce9578e01e19f11a846b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc25d09f19797d7b290144c34c7eb8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2c13e4dc0c5ffdeff6ad422bae25f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2fe3a0bbcef55cf31ca985ee9806595&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5667e6d6ac2a6898d54282e5227a0e3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea00e0f2c81dc0fc8cf34f9d8c29edd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13d0c437f60ca3acd04da12cb2b56d6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c1010a5001bece4042095877f6a8d42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81c9e21c9bd682aec8ed5433b29254d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e2d16d0dd871aa1289650bde0921622&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5877d488b5991002f2148f74e454ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9993599a98c4a13ce90be07d75f3c76e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-822eea5aa72002e3d106bf0be08669dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eead988a81ce4ca9e3ae8f503d1cfe1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34990b1b85de7de8bbd3a8165873d9e7</data>
