    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COUNTER VARIABLES CNT1 AND CNT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SIMULATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"cnt1 counts reachable non-zero cells (land), cnt2 counts adjacent zero cells (water) in each BFS component, simulating the process of mapping connected regions and their boundaries."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4117c59b410de1711656865bd10cb59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONTROL_STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"dx is an array defining the horizontal displacement for four directional moves (right, left, up, down) in the BFS grid traversal, used to explore neighboring cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4117c59b410de1711656865bd10cb59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONTROL_STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"dy is an array defining the vertical displacement for four directional moves (right, left, up, down) in the BFS grid traversal, used in conjunction with dx to navigate adjacent cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4117c59b410de1711656865bd10cb59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"VARIABLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A 2D array used to represent a grid or matrix in the code, where elements are accessed via indices i, j, and k to evaluate conditions related to the problem logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"a is a 2D integer array representing the grid, where each cell holds a value of 0 or 1, encoding land (1) and water (0) for graph traversal and component analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"a 是题目中用于表示连续子串的符号变量，代表长度为k的连续字符序列。"&lt;SEP&gt;"a是代表一个n位二进制数的变量，作为位运算操作的对象之一，需通过反置或交换位操作以满足a⊕b=c的条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"a 是一个 n 位二进制数，作为操作对象之一，可通过反置或交换位来调整，目标是使其与 b 异或后等于 c。"&lt;SEP&gt;"a 是一个 n 位二进制数，作为位运算操作的目标之一，其位可被翻转或交换以满足 a⊕b=c 的条件。"&lt;SEP&gt;"a is a binary number of n bits, one of the two operands in the XOR operation a⊕b=c, subject to bit-flip and bit-swap operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"a 是一个 n 位二进制数，作为位运算操作的目标之一，可通过翻转或交换位来改变其值，目标是使 a⊕b=c 成立。"&lt;SEP&gt;"a is a binary number of n bits, one of the two operands in the XOR operation a⊕b=c, subject to bit-flip and bit-swap operations to minimize cost."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c558efa82eea3b35fae76cbadb1eff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2076568b2623a983fd25582f3fa50c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51b47f04a5032a9117dced97c6aa7a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e96fe33a652d98236ab6e39e9022dc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-740455e328e2f67f25cee018470473d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337f6c50a6fc0269c78db8502813c381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4117c59b410de1711656865bd10cb59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f44ccaba75ddd991df3ba87881e905b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-545d80205967186bbfce4955f69aa723</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONTROL_STRUCTURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"vis is a 2D boolean array used to mark visited cells during BFS, ensuring each node is processed only once to prevent cycles and redundant computation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a4117c59b410de1711656865bd10cb59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;F&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A boolean flag variable used in nested loops to track whether any element in a row or column exceeds 1; incorrectly reset or not properly scoped, leading to logical errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"A boolean flag variable used to track whether any element in a row or column exceeds 1, incorrectly reset or misused in nested loops leading to logical errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"f is a nested map structure used to track whether a zero cell (water) has been counted as an adjacent boundary cell, preventing duplicate counting via hash-based lookup."&lt;SEP&gt;"A boolean flag variable used to track whether any element in a row or column exceeds 1, influencing the final value of 'flag'."</data>
