      <data key="d1">"This line allocates more space than needed for the string s, suggesting a potential off-by-one or buffer allocation misunderstanding in the student’s implementation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOR(INT I = 1; I &lt;= N - M; ++ I) S[I] = (CHAR)('A' + I - 1)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This loop attempts to construct a prefix of distinct characters, but starts at index 1 and uses 1-based indexing inconsistently with C++ 0-based arrays, risking undefined behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOR(INT I = N; I &gt; M; -- I) S[I] = (CHAR)('A' + N - I)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This loop attempts to construct a suffix with decreasing characters, but may overwrite earlier characters due to overlapping index ranges and 1-based assumptions, leading to incorrect string construction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
    </node>
