    <node id="&quot;TIC-TAC-TOE GAME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tic-Tac-Toe Game is a 3x3 grid-based, turn-based strategic contest between 小L and 炸鸡, in which players alternately place X and O marks with the objective of aligning three of their own marks in a row, column, or diagonal. The game is currently in an unresolved mid-game state, with both players having made an equal number of moves and no winner yet determined. Despite variations in terminology across sources—such as “drawn state,” “mid-state,” or “残局 (residual position)” —all descriptions consistently agree on the core conditions: balanced move counts, no victor, and an active, ongoing game. It is now 小L’s turn to play, and 小L holds a unique, one-time special privilege to make two consecutive moves during this single turn. This double-move privilege represents a significant deviation from standard tic-tac-toe rules, granting 小L an exceptional strategic advantage to potentially secure victory or block 炸鸡’s winning opportunities in a single action. The game remains entirely undecided, and its outcome hinges entirely on 小L’s forthcoming dual moves, making this moment a critical turning point in the contest.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-478ef0557cc0427a88aeac7c8e7fd593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd4eda16155c0a4cb6a2357257e23c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5877d488b5991002f2148f74e454ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c81dadb0077742b9e0c42699623a7c2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1ff29e648a8e199ea54e1d3f51e580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b3750f193faab9aceaa89b9df470e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-183a7f24059ae22698c59d6bce91789e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;3X3 GRID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 3x3 grid is the playing board of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j) where i is the row and j is the column, and each cell can hold 'X', 'O', or 'G' to represent player moves or empty spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing board of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j), where i is the row (1-3) and j is the column (1-3). Each cell can contain 'X', 'O', or 'G' representing player moves or empty spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing board of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j), where i is the row (1–3) and j is the column (1–3). Each cell can hold 'X', 'O', or 'G' to represent moves or empty spaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing field of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of 9 cells arranged in 3 rows and 3 columns, where players place their marks to achieve three in a line."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 3x3 grid is the playing board of the tic-tac-toe game, consisting of nine cells identified by coordinates (i,j), where i is the row (1 to 3) and j is the column (1 to 3). Each cell can contain 'X', 'O', or 'G' representing player marks or empty spaces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b3750f193faab9aceaa89b9df470e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'O' is the symbol used to represent a move made by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 grid, indicating their placed mark in a cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' is the symbol used to represent 炸鸡's moves on the 3x3 grid, indicating ownership of a cell in the tic-tac-toe game."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents the mark placed by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 board, indicating one of the opponent's moves in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' is the symbol used to represent moves made by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 grid, indicating ownership of a cell in the tic-tac-toe game."&lt;SEP&gt;"O represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating one of the opponent's moves in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents the mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating one of their moves in a cell."&lt;SEP&gt;"O represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating one of the opponent's moves in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"O represents a mark placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating one of the opponent's moves in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"O is a symbol representing a move made by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, occupying one of the nine grid positions."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents the symbol placed by 炸鸡 on the tic-tac-toe board, indicating their moves in the 3x3 grid."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' is the symbol used to represent moves made by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 grid, indicating ownership of a cell in the tic-tac-toe game."&lt;SEP&gt;"'O' represents the symbol placed by 炸鸡 on the 3x3 board, indicating one of their moves in the game."</data>
