    <edge source="&quot;中国&quot;" target="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">106.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Student Program is written in C++ with Chinese-style competitive programming conventions (e.g., #define pb push_back, use of std::cin.tie), consistent with Chinese OI training practices."&lt;SEP&gt;The Student Program is written in C++ and exhibits a distinct set of coding conventions and contextual elements that strongly indicate its origin within China’s competitive programming education ecosystem, particularly in environments such as ACM/NOI (National Olympiad in Informatics). The program features a Chinese-language problem context, Chinese-style variable comments, and variable naming practices commonly seen in Chinese programming contests—such as short identifiers like 'n', 'm', 'cnti', 'cntj', and abbreviations like 'pb' (push_back), 'fi' (first), 'se' (second), and 'PI' (often used for pi or as a macro). It also employs standard C++ competitive programming idioms prevalent in China, including the macro definition #define int long long to avoid overflow issues, and optimizations like std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false) for faster I/O. These stylistic and syntactic choices are not merely technical preferences but reflect deeply embedded norms within China’s coding competition culture, where such practices are systematically taught and reinforced in educational settings. The consistent presence of Chinese-language annotations and problem statements across multiple descriptions confirms that the program was developed in a Chinese-speaking academic or competitive programming environment, aligning with the broader norms of China’s programming education system. Thus, the Student Program is unequivocally rooted in the Chinese competitive programming tradition, both in its technical implementation and cultural context.</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-ead7e34b7b56278b26df573c33612322&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ab516531ae70002b07e7282cf9f96ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e9224b862712b828a49a7af0256744a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0569105254caf9ef1ed75024750e2dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa0781f7cefac10e68ae2462b8b87c96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b4052fa7b1e85dd77092d52fe9cb8b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c230135cc0686d17fd15b2cc48624237&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c9ab832b90cad70f560049e7a740427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c900fee450edfcc61df8a5dc49da1d44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bb812737ccf1fcdbc2dc32333a9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-149cbf20a38db662126124752f186e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6498d4b9b73c6042d086d98534de214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ba71498d3f8470570296343c8c189b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf87c7e9ad9d433d6f2ea0161bd510c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87a87454ea6eb00654ad5366c5971784</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
