    <edge source="&quot;STUDENT PROGRAM&quot;" target="&quot;GREEDY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">79.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Student Program uses a greedy strategy by assigning the smallest available integer l to each interval in sorted order, directly implementing a greedy approach."&lt;SEP&gt;"The commented greedy logic shows the student understood the optimal strategy for this problem but failed to implement it correctly."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student uses a greedy assignment strategy by incrementing the smallest available number and assigning it to the first compatible interval, which is a direct application of the Greedy knowledge point."&lt;SEP&gt;"The program uses a greedy strategy to place each '1' into the nearest available position in the target quadrant without considering global optimality, which is logically sound but may contain implementation flaws."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student uses a greedy approach—immediately moving each '1' to the next available position in the top-left quadrant without considering global configuration—leading to potential errors in swap sequence validity."&lt;SEP&gt;"The algorithm greedily moves each '1' to the nearest valid position in the top-left quadrant as soon as it is encountered, without lookahead or optimization — a correct greedy approach given the problem’s guarantee of a solution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student employs a greedy strategy by moving each '1' to the nearest target position in order, without considering global rearrangement efficiency, leading to incorrect final configurations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student uses a greedy approach to move each '1' to the top-left quadrant as soon as possible, which is the intended strategy, but the implementation violates the greedy assumption by not maintaining invariant positions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student uses a greedy character assignment strategy (distinct letters in prefix, repeated 'a' in middle, reverse in suffix), but this greedy method does not guarantee the existence of the required non-contiguous subsequence, leading to incorrect outputs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The algorithm greedily moves each '1' to the next available target position in the top-left quadrant without reconsidering prior moves, indicating a greedy strategy."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-4bfa74d3cde642ef5d69d9445bbe6168&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3265a331ceecdcaa4effe7d518de46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-522813e50d2e43c2f3a90462ea89a27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0569105254caf9ef1ed75024750e2dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57aa2fab03045a4f1a94b22bda9b2d8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-751de14de4f6fd0795902684f69fa4d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bb812737ccf1fcdbc2dc32333a9c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-149cbf20a38db662126124752f186e78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6498d4b9b73c6042d086d98534de214&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b114d72fb1df4b15a6815afb987ada0</data>
