      <data key="d3">92.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Simulation of swaps relies on control structures (loops, conditionals) to track positions and manage the state transitions of the matrix during transformation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simulations rely heavily on control structures to model step-by-step state transitions and decision logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures (loops and conditionals) correctly iterate over the grid, but the simulation logic inside them is flawed, indicating that while control flow is understood, the simulated algorithm is not."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation of diagonal traversal relies on precise control structures (while loops with coordinate updates), demonstrating that simulation is implemented through structured control flow."&lt;SEP&gt;"The if-else control structure enables the simulation of two distinct computational paths based on condition evaluation, which is central to the problem's logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student uses control structures (if-statements, loops) to simulate a grid-based condition evaluation, indicating an attempt to model a system through iterative logic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation of grid-based rules relies heavily on control structures like if-statements and flags to determine state changes, indicating tight integration between simulation logic and conditional control."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation of grid-based rules relies heavily on nested control structures (loops and conditionals) to evaluate and update the flag based on adjacency conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student uses control structures (if, for loops) to implement a simulation of matrix-based conditions, but the logic in the condition a[k][3 - k + 1] &gt; 1 is flawed, indicating misunderstanding of the intended simulation rule."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control structures (loops and conditionals) are used to implement a simulation of grid pattern validation, indicating that control flow enables the simulation logic."</data>
