      <data key="d4">"Although diagonal sums are stored in sum2[], no dynamic programming recurrence is used to compute optimal paths or values — the simulation is purely additive, not optimization-driven."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student attempts to combine simulation (iterative matrix traversal) with dynamic programming (memoizing sums), but confuses the two by misapplying DP state updates within a simulation framework, leading to logical errors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The problem structure suggests a potential dynamic programming intent (overlapping subproblems in grid validation), but the student’s brute-force simulation fails to leverage memoization or optimal substructure, leading to inefficiency and possible incorrectness."&lt;SEP&gt;"The simulation logic attempts to track state changes using flags, resembling dynamic programming, but fails to properly define or store subproblem solutions, revealing a flawed application."</data>
