      <data key="d3">63.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The student is the author of the erroneous code that triggered the error description, demonstrating misunderstanding in control structures and simulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student provides the error description to explain their reasoning, which helps the evaluator interpret their level of understanding."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student's submission generated the error description, which reflects their level of comprehension or misconception."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student's incorrect submission generated the error description, which is used to evaluate their understanding of the problem."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student submitted a program that triggered the error description due to flawed logic in array condition checks and flag management."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student’s submission generates an error description that is analyzed to classify their understanding as 'Good:' or 'Bad:'."&lt;SEP&gt;"The student’s submission generates an error description that is used to assess their understanding or misunderstanding of the problem."</data>
