    <edge source="&quot;小苯&quot;" target="&quot;NUMBER_THEORY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">24.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"小苯 misunderstands the relationship between XOR and GCD, incorrectly assuming that if j divides a_i, then gcd(a_i, j) = j and a_i XOR j = j implies the condition — a fundamental number-theoretic error."&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯's code incorrectly assumes divisor relationships imply the XOR-GCD equality without validating the deeper number-theoretic properties required, showing a significant gap in understanding the mathematical foundation."&lt;SEP&gt;"小苯's solution attempts to leverage the mathematical relationship between XOR and GCD, a core number theory concept, though the implementation contains logical errors in pair validation."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c0621f867e87fb25088a534465259d65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff32fffb52415ec4221990a56352b068&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d78f2079f220a0196b9a21caa622db85</data>
