    <edge source="&quot;EVALUATOR&quot;" target="&quot;KNOWLEDGE POINT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The evaluator maps each knowledge point to the student’s submission to determine whether it was demonstrated correctly ('Good') or incorrectly ('Bad')."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-a074a38ecf5866008803eb9d3c6559bb</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KNOWLEDGE POINT&quot;" target="&quot;GOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"A knowledge point is considered mastered when the 'Good' indicator is applied to a submission, meaning no errors were detected related to that concept."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 'Good' marker indicates that the student has correctly understood the associated knowledge point, as no errors were reported."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-0e25d2145ec23366f1eef2a7d47f3400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26b0d0ed2ff7cae6f89f08cce6fe3a3e</data>
