    <edge source="&quot;A.CPP&quot;" target="&quot;ERROR: EXPECTED PRIMARY-EXPRESSION BEFORE ‘,’ TOKEN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The malformed declaration 'int n = , m;' directly causes this syntax error, indicating a fundamental misunderstanding of C++ variable initialization syntax."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A.CPP&quot;" target="&quot;CNT = STD::MIN(0LL , 2 * M - N)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The expression uses min(0ll, ...) which will always be non-positive, rendering the loop for repeating 'a' ineffective, showing a logical flaw in the construction algorithm."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A.CPP&quot;" target="&quot;FOR(INT I = 1; I &lt;= N - M; ++ I) S[I] = (CHAR)('A' + I - 1)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The use of 1-based indexing on a C++ string (0-based) may cause buffer overflow or incorrect character placement, indicating a misunderstanding of array indexing."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;A.CPP&quot;" target="&quot;FOR(INT I = N; I &gt; M; -- I) S[I] = (CHAR)('A' + N - I)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"This loop writes into indices n down to m+1, potentially overwriting the prefix built earlier, leading to incorrect string structure and loveliness."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SUBSTRING&quot;" target="&quot;NON-CONTIGUOUS SUBSEQUENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Both must be of equal length k and identical in content to satisfy the loveliness condition a=b, forming the core logical constraint."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ERROR: EXPECTED PRIMARY-EXPRESSION BEFORE ‘,’ TOKEN&quot;" target="&quot;ERROR: ‘M’ WAS NOT DECLARED IN THIS SCOPE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The first syntax error prevents the compiler from recognizing m as a declared variable, causing the second error — a direct cascading failure."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-9b7fdb13d220397bc7332d07c7cfc57e</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
