    <edge source="&quot;炸鸡&quot;" target="&quot;TIC-TAC-TOE GAME&quot;">
      <data key="d3">129.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"炸鸡 is an opponent in the tic-tac-toe game who, despite overconfidence, enforces the rules and plays optimally to counter 小L's advantage."&lt;SEP&gt;The Tic-Tac-Toe Game involves two players: 小L and 炸鸡, with 炸鸡 serving as the opposing player who designed and instituted a rule modification granting 小L the privilege of double moves. 炸鸡 introduced this special rule under the belief that it would be a harmless concession, neither compromising their own winning chances nor undermining their strategic superiority. Despite this apparent advantage given to 小L, 炸鸡 remains confident in their superior skill and strategic acumen, expecting to neutralize the double-move benefit through expert play. Multiple descriptions emphasize that 炸鸡’s decision reflects overconfidence—yet it is also a deliberate and strategic act, indicating deep engagement with the game’s dynamics. By setting the terms of play, including the double-move rule, 炸鸡 has inadvertently shifted the game’s strategic balance, creating a complex scenario where their own overconfidence has become a defining feature of the match. Thus, 炸鸡 is not merely a passive opponent but an active architect of the game’s unique conditions, whose actions—though rooted in self-assuredness—have significantly influenced the evolving strategic landscape of the Tic-Tac-Toe Game.&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player in the tic-tac-toe game who has introduced a strategic imbalance by granting 小L a two-move privilege."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 is the opposing player in the tic-tac-toe game who, despite being strategically superior, allows a privilege that may alter the game's outcome."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-478ef0557cc0427a88aeac7c8e7fd593&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd4eda16155c0a4cb6a2357257e23c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5877d488b5991002f2148f74e454ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c81dadb0077742b9e0c42699623a7c2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e1ff29e648a8e199ea54e1d3f51e580&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b3750f193faab9aceaa89b9df470e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-183a7f24059ae22698c59d6bce91789e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;炸鸡&quot;" target="&quot;O&quot;">
      <data key="d3">110.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"O is the marker used by 炸鸡 to denote their moves on the tic-tac-toe board, directly representing 炸鸡's actions in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"O is the symbol used by 炸鸡 to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board, directly representing 炸鸡's actions in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"O is the symbol used by 炸鸡 to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board, directly representing 炸鸡's actions in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"O is the symbol used by 炸鸡 to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board, directly representing 炸鸡's actions in the game."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 uses the 'O' symbol to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 uses the symbol 'O' to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe grid, establishing direct ownership and identity of their plays."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 uses the symbol 'O' to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe grid, making 'O' a direct representation of their actions."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 uses the symbol 'O' to mark their moves on the 3x3 grid in the tic-tac-toe game."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 uses the 'O' symbol to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 uses the symbol 'O' to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 uses the symbol 'O' to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe grid, establishing direct ownership and identity of their plays."&lt;SEP&gt;"炸鸡 uses the 'O' symbol to mark their moves on the tic-tac-toe board."</data>
      <data key="d5">chunk-c65c413a0785f44cfb35456d545b19d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-649cc18b2d0fdb15683c43c49f191a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-054c255dec239c2762b373ecc1e4a1e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc16b5f321438c090a3a2ab6291f38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf315318fb9435781f726121555b7204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b256fd1c0676b66deece8e4e49ff37e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f761857c7438d0e8234494cb00c030e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b3750f193faab9aceaa89b9df470e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34feb8b38494b33de0e8d583302bc5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a376d30d059b09f44ce6681d11e112d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea15e123e23c10fb0dd1d2aa46c0de25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65da65cd36531d031db5b8f1d3d85dab</data>
      <data key="d6">1</data>
    </edge>
